```plaintext
1result.sql
```

Reason:
• 0result.sql rounds the average composition to four decimals before selecting the monthly winner, so the three‑month rolling averages are slightly off (e.g. 11‑2018 and 06‑2019 differ by 0.0001).  
• Both 1result.sql and 2result.sql keep full precision until the final display and therefore return the exact maxima and correct rolling averages.  
• Between those two, 1result.sql is the clearer and more direct solution: it relies on the existing numeric _year and _month columns for ordering/filtering instead of parsing month_year text, avoids unnecessary string manipulation, and uses straightforward CTE steps.